## calendars

calendars-ask = Shakespeare and Cervantes died on 23 April 1616. On the same day?
calendars-title = Calendars old and new
calendars-question = A calendar counts whole days, and the seasons go by the Sun: from one spring equinox to the next 365.24219 days pass — not a whole number. We model calendars old and new and see how they keep up with the Sun. And at the end, a riddle: William Shakespeare and Miguel de Cervantes both died on 23 April 1616. On the same day?
calendars-choices = Yes, on the same day — the date is the same
calendars-choices-2 = Nearly: a few hours apart, by the time zones
calendars-choices-3 = No, more than ten days apart
calendars-setup = A table of calendars (the length of the year in each), the length of the year by the Sun — from equinox to equinox, a counter of years; calendar sheets of 1582 and 1616
